Hyper Param Optimizer
=====================

Overview
--------

This code is a work in progress...

Find the best set of hyperparameters given both physical (e.g. lattice param, cohesiev energy) and hyperparameters (e.g. cutoff distance, basis function width/position) constraints.
Currently interfaced with LAMMPS to calculate physical quantities.

Requires two config files to run:
1. The usual config file used for training (see manual for more detail)
2. The targets config file - where we specify all contraints

Format of targets config file
-----------------------------

The format is similar to the training config file.
It contains a list of KEYS followed by VALUES. Each key is listed on a new line.
'#' can be used to comment out a line.
The order in which KEY-VALUES are listed does not matter. 
Every KEY belongs to one of the three groups: General, Hyper or Physical

General:
MAXSCORE
ERMSE
MAXCALLS
EPS

Hyper:
CONFIGMAP
CONFIGMIN
CONFIGMAX

Physical:
LATA
ECOH
EVACF
HVACF
SURFACE
ELASTIC

Format for KEY-VALUE(S)
---------------------

General:
MAXSCORE <int> N
ERMSE <float> V 
MAXCALLS <int> N
EPS <float> V

Hyper:
CONFIGMAP param_1 param_2 param_3 ...
CONFIGMIN minval_1 minval_2 minval_3 ...
CONFIGMAX maxval_1 maxval_2 maxval_3 ...

example:
CONFIGMAP  RCUT2B CGRID2B SGRID2B SGRID2B SGRID2B
CONFIGMIN  4.4    1.1     0.11    0.12    1.13
CONFIGMAX  6.0    6.0     4.01    4.02    4.03


Optimisable hyperparameters:
    - RCUT2B
    - RCUTMB
    - SGRID2B
    - SGRIDMB
    - CGRID2B
    - CGRIDMB

Physical:

    - LATA <float> a      # target lattice parameter (A) for cubic cell only
    - ECOH <float> E_c    # target cohesieve energy (eV)
    - EVACF <float,float,float> P (GPa), a (A), E_vf (eV)
      # Pressure, lattice param, target vacancy formation energy (eV)
    - HVACF <float,float,float> P (GPa), a (A), H_vf (eV)
      # Pressure, lattice param, target vacancy formation enthalpy (eV)
    - SURFACE <int,float> hkl E_hkl    # hkl surface, target surface energy (eV)
    - ELASTIC <int,float> ij C_ij 
      # Elastic constatnts tensor component (Voigt notation),
        target stress value (GPa)


Requirements
------------

    - lammps compiled as linkable dynamic library
    - some kind of optimizer, tested with dlib library (dlib::find_min_global)
    - compiled with mpi so use mpic++ or mpi wrapper
    - link all necessary libraries, e.g.
      (-ldlib -lcblas -llapack -lpthread -fopenmp -ltadah -llammps_serial)
    - arguably is is easier to compile using CMake, see example
    - config.train file and target config present in the run dir


Example
-------

See example ex_hpo_1 in the 'examples' in the project directory.
